-- title:
--   Gauss subring of K lies over that of K₀ (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Inside $\operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ consider two intermediate fields over $L$: $K$, assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) $L$ of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) $(q^2M')$ $H$ with $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) $q$ $M'$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units $\equiv 1 \bmod q$ — that is, the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_f)/\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_g) \ne 0$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$; and $K_0$, assumed equal to the same base change of the analogous $q$-expansion field for $\Gamma_0(M')$, with $K_0 \le K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\operatorname{Frac} A = L$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ and $O_0$ one of $K_0$, each characterised by the same Gauss condition: $f$ belongs to it precisely when there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal and $f \cdot y = x$ in $\operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ after applying $A \to L$ coefficientwise. Then, for the $K_0$-algebra structure on $K$ given by the inclusion, an element $x \in K_0$ has $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,x \in W_0$ if and only if $x \in O_0$.
--
--   This says that the Gauss (Igusa-type) valuation subring attached to $A$-integral $q$-expansions on the level $q^2M'$ curve $X_H$, with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$, restricts on the $\Gamma_0(M')$ floor to the corresponding Gauss subring there, so that $W_0$ lies over $O_0$; it is the $q = 3$ case of this compatibility. It feeds the construction of a local homomorphism with separable residue field extension at the cusp branch in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isLocalHom_and_isSeparable_residueField_of_eq_comap_gauss_of_levelH_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isLocalHom_and_isSeparable_residueField_of_eq_comap_gauss_of_levelH_of_eq_three).
